==Trivia==
*Dead Donny Dash is very likely based off of [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Kitarō|Kitarō]], the titular protagonist of ''[[wikipedia:GeGeGe no Kitarō|GeGeGe no Kitarō]]''. The most obvious similarity is their hairstyles, but there are multiple other connections as well:
**Both come from the grave: Donny is a Zombie enemy introduced in [[Inviting Cemetary]], while Kitarō was born in a cemetery.
**Donny attacks by kicking his shoes at [[Cat Units]] and having them reappear on his feet, which is similar to how Kitarō uses his weaponized [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Geta|Geta]] sandals.
**The ''GeGeGe no Kitarō'' opening theme mentions "[[Sports Night (Monthly Event)|sports festivals in the graveyard at night]]".
**The smoking gun is that Donny's first name in Japanese is Shitarō (死太郎); this is spelled and pronounced identically to Kitarō (鬼太郎), except that it swaps ''ki'' (鬼) with ''shi'' (死), meaning "death".
***Incidentally, the first [[Sports Night (Monthly Event)|Sports Night]] event ended the day before [[Yuru-i GeGeGe no Kitarou: Youkai Dotabata Daisensou]] was released.
***His Japanese name may additionally be a reference to ''[[wikipedia:Dash! Yonkuro|Dash! Yonkuro]]'', as ダッシュ死太郎 is not that far off from ダッシュ!四駆郎.

